diff --git a/docs/src/platform-support.md b/docs/src/platform-support.md
index fd80e7b..b90f1f1 100644
--- a/docs/src/platform-support.md
+++ b/docs/src/platform-support.md
@@ -46,0 +47,21 @@ The `rust-gpu` project currently supports a limited number of platforms and grap
+#### experimental 64-bit pointer ABI
+
+Append `-physical64` to a Vulkan target, for example
+`spirv-unknown-vulkan1.3-physical64`, to select eight-byte Rust pointers and
+`usize`. This is an explicit ABI choice made before rustc computes layouts or
+lowers casts. All existing targets retain four-byte pointers and `usize`.
+`u32` stays four bytes and `u64` stays eight bytes on both kinds of target.
+Capabilities alone do not change the Rust ABI.
+
+Build the shader and its dependencies for the same target. The builder's target
+JSON and the compiler's expected target must agree exactly, including pointer
+width and data layout. Do not reuse layouts containing `usize` or raw pointers
+across the two ABIs. An explicit `u64` address field avoids depending on the
+host's pointer width, but does not establish that an address is valid to access.
+
+This initial target support only establishes Rust layout and integer behavior.
+Integer-pointer casts remain rejected, and selecting this target does not yet
+enable physical memory operations or change logical storage classes. Physical
+addressing, alignment and alias rules require separate lowering and validation.
+The layout compiletests do not execute shaders or dereference synthetic values.
+
